xnu 0418: kern.sweet_fb_copy2x: a 2x frame that is copied goes 1:1 into a flip buffer and the plane scales it

A frame of the window server that cannot be scanned out (a surface outside the pool, one swapped again while on the
panel, the ring held to the copy by 0354) is copied by the GPU's 2D engine into a flip buffer of the panel's size:
two bilinear half passes from 720 x 1600 to 1080 x 2400, 10.4 MB written and ~4.15 ms of GPU a frame (lab log M11),
and the plane shows the flip buffer unscaled. A frame scanned out leaves the plane scaled over the surface: between the
two ways the plane's 27 registers change, and the picture is filtered by different hardware.

With kern.sweet_fb_copy2x=1 (boot-arg sweetfb_copy2x=1; 0 by default) presentQueued() asks present() for the
scanout's own window of the 2x picture (sweet_scan_window(): 720 x 1600 from 16,12 on this phone) copied 1:1 into the
back flip buffer with rows of 2880 bytes (45 x 64: one pass, the source rectangle as large as the destination). The
queued frame carries that geometry (0, 0, 720, 1600) and its pitch, and frameShow() flips it with planeScaled(), as a
frame of a surface: VIG0's QSEED3lite scales it onto the panel. With a linear surface the plane's geometry is the same
in the two ways (presentScanout() crops the window by the address) and only SRC0_ADDR and the row pitch change; after
a UBWC frame, planeScaled() with no queued frame gives the plane its linear registers back (0410) and SRC_XY changes.
A UBWC source is decompressed by 0415's blit, 1:1.

The flip buffers are the same three (a 2x window fits in one, 4.6 of 10.4 MB); the console, the boot frame and display
off still flip them unscaled through scanFrom(), which sets the plane back (planeUnscaled()). The 1:1 copy is not
asked for where the plane cannot scale: no 2x drawing, sweet_fb_scan_ready not set by start(), or a flush of the
scaled plane not taken (fScanStuck). A window that does not fit is copied x1.5 as before. The queue waits for a
writable plane before such a flip, as for a frame of a surface.

kern.sweet_fb_scanout_diag: "0418: 1:1 copies scaled by the plane (kern.sweet_fb_copy2x N): made, flipped, window not
fit". Expected [estimate, 03-diseno-pool-y-copia.md B1]: 1.5-2 ms of GPU a copied frame instead of 4.15; not measured
yet (kern.sweet_gpu_marks=1, protocol in 18-presentacion-y-dpu/04-parches-0417-0418.md).
